0007-xlsx-outline: row/column outlines (grouping) for the xlsx engine.

- xlsx-model: SheetOutline (outlineLevel per row/col, summaryBelow/Right) as
  read-only base data, parsed in xlsx-parse/read.rs. Not part of the CRDT.
- Collapse/expand = batches of the existing SetRow/ColVisibility ops (synced,
  undoable). `collapsed` on the summary row/col is derived from the hidden
  state on save, on both the source-patch and the full writer paths.
- xlsx-render GridMeta: rowOutline/colOutline runs [first,last,level] and
  outlineSummaryAbove/Left, so hosts can draw an outline gutter.
- xlsx-react: `outlineVisibility {axis,sheet,indices,hidden}` command, one
  applyOps batch (one undo step, one sync update).
- Upstream defaults unchanged; a malformed outlineLevel reads as ungrouped;
  SheetOutline is excluded from Sheet equality.

KNOWN LIMITS
1. Nested restore is lossy: collapse an outer group while an inner one is open,
   then expand the outer: the inner comes back collapsed (Excel restores it
   open). Pinned by tests/outline.rs.
2. Outline levels do not follow row/col inserts or deletes (gutter and
   full-writer saves); the patch path copies source row/col tags verbatim.

